i made this painting which is a copy of  fangirl's story night what this depicts  is the view from the window of a mental  health facility van gogh was struggling  a lot with his mental health  and one of the times that he admitted  himself he looked out of the window and  painted his interpretation of what he  saw  this has since become one of the most  well recognized paintings of all time  but sadly the incredible story behind it  is just  lost when i was younger i used to try to  imagine what it must have felt like for  him being locked up voluntarily  with no certainty for his future and  completely alone and  yet he managed at the lowest point in  his life  to look out of the window and see beauty  in the world the reason i think this is  the best painting out there is that it  represents insightfulness into one's own  condition  it represents the desire of someone to  improve and get better  and it also represents the ability to  see beauty in everything it also reminds  me that masterpieces can be born in the  hardest times  for that reason this painting has come  with me to every single house that i've  been living in  since and it is one of the most  inspirational pieces of art in my  collection i generally hope that you are  safe happy and well
 

